---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import InstallTabs from '../components/InstallTabs.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';
const entries = (await getCollection('install'));
---
<Base title="Install" description="Install the Specstride plugin in Claude Code, with its prerequisites, and run it on a ready-made example first.">
  <div class="wrap page">
    <p class="eyebrow mono">// install</p>
    <h1>Install</h1>
    <p class="lede">Commands are run by hand, exactly as written; the date under the path says when it was last verified that way.</p>
    <InstallTabs entries={entries} full id="install-page" headingLevel="h2" />
    <h2 class="next">After the first run</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Something look off? The <code>specstride-doctor</code> skill checks this machine: it runs the doctor, lists each finding with its fix, and installs nothing.</li>
      <li>To end a run cleanly, use the <code>stop</code> verb of the <code>specstride</code> CLI that the plugin bundles: the run ends at the next safe boundary, the record closes whole, no survivor.</li>
      <li>Settings live in your user configuration, <code>~/.config/specstride/config.yaml</code> — parallel units are turned on there, and with several features in <code>specs/</code> you set <code>SPECSTRIDE_FEATURE</code> to the directory name.</li>
      <li>Every error a run can print, with its fix, is in the wiki's <a href={`${SITE.repoUrl}/blob/main/wiki/Troubleshooting.md`}>Troubleshooting</a> page.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .page { padding-top: var(--space-7); }
  .eyebrow { color: var(--accent); font-size: var(--step--1); margin-bottom: var(--space-2); }
  .lede { margin-bottom: var(--space-6); color: var(--muted); }
  .next { margin-top: var(--space-8); }
</style>
